// run
// #5173: JSXChildExpression's Expression is OPTIONAL (SPEC §12.12) - both
// `{}` and the standard `{/* comment */}` idiom parse and contribute NO
// child, against the REAL pkg/web library. `parseJsxChildBraced`
// (parserjsx.bit) still builds a `Tag.JsxExpr` node for an empty `{}` (a
// bare `return 0` here silently deleted the brace pair on the next `bit
// fmt`, this file's first shape); `jsxChildValues` (desugarjsx.bit) is what
// drops it before `elem`/`attr` ever sees it, so `bit run` proves the
// render has neither placeholder, not just that the parse succeeds. `bit
// fmt` relocates a comment written INSIDE `{}` to just after the element
// (its own gap, tracked separately, not this ticket's) - both `{}` below
// started life as one bare and one holding `/* a trailing note, not a
// child */` before that pass; the canonical form checked in here is what
// `bit fmt` itself produces from that source.
import { render, elem, text } from "../../pkg/web"

fn main() {
  let page = <div>a{}b{}c</div> /* a trailing note, not a child */
  println(render(page))
}
